+# OR(2)-weak research report
+
+Date: 2026-10-18. Status: **WORK IN PROGRESS**; this file is an interim checkpoint.
+
+## Exact assignment and conventions
+
+Let `t` be a positive integer and `S` a finite nonempty subset of the positive
+integers satisfying `S ∩ (S + jt) = ∅` for `j = ±1, ±2`. Put
+`A = S ∪ (S+t)`, `n = |S|`, and
+`M(A) = -min_{x∈R} Σ_{a∈A} cos(ax)`.
+The target is a proved natural subclass, a quantitative conditional structural
+theorem, or a rigorously certified obstruction to
+`M(A) ≥ c n^(1/4+δ)` for absolute `c,δ>0`.
+
+## Starting frontier (read, not claimed as new)
+
+- **PROVED in the project record:** the dilated full-section rotation sweep;
+  the localization inequality P24; the group O4 obstruction to a group-only
+  improvement. Read `.research/NOTEBOOK.md`, especially “Where a Z-specific
+  run-top bound must come from,” and the surrounding OR(2) reassessment.
+- **PROVED limitation of scope:** P24's bounded multiplicative spread
+  corollary is already in the record and would not be new progress.
+- **CONJECTURED / unresolved here:** unrestricted OR(2)-weak in `Z`.
+
+## Current attacks and first falsification tests
+
+1. Extend the free rotation mechanism from one exact dilate to a thin union of
+   residue classes / approximately periodic sets. Track the phase error rather
+   than claiming that localization separates the two copies.
+2. Use the exact zero `1+exp(itx)=0` to derive derivative or local positivity
+   constraints on the sine component. Check whether these give more than the
+   existing energy bound.
+3. Seek a quantitative obstruction to simultaneous one-sided Fourier behavior
+   at all continuous twists; any result will state the required quantitative
+   structure explicitly.
+
+No new theorem is claimed at this checkpoint. All substantive computations will
+run only on `dirichlet` using `src/dirun.sh -c 3` or less. Only this report and
+files in `.research/agents/or2_scratch/` will be edited; no commits will be made.
+
+## Interim derivation: a candidate quantitative subclass theorem
+
+**CONJECTURED pending adversarial verification of the proof below:** Let
+`R ⊂ {0,…,floor(t/2)}`, `k=|R|≥1`, and for each `r∈R` let `Y_r` be a finite
+subset of `Z_{≥1}`. Set `S=⋃_r(qY_r+r)`, `n=Σ_r |Y_r|≥1`. If
+`q≥40t√k`, then
+
+`M(S∪(S+t)) ≥ √n/(72√k)`.
+
+The expected proof lifts the sum to
+`h_θ(u)=Re[(1+e^{itu})Σ_r e^{iru}F_{Y_r}(θ)]`. For each fixed `θ`, the
+original bound `f_A≥−M` holds at the `q` macro-grid points
+`u=(θ+2πj)/q`, because `qu≡θ (mod 2π)`. With
+`Z(θ)^2=Σ_r |F_{Y_r}(θ)|²`, `U=2√k Z`, `D=t+max R`, one has
+`|h_θ''|≤D²U`. Taylor expansion at a global minimum gives
+`h_θ≥−M−εU`, where `ε=π²D²/(2q²)`.
+
+At the exact macro-zero `u₀=π/t`,
+`h_θ(u₀)=0` and `h_θ'(u₀)=t Im Σ_r e^{irπ/t}F_{Y_r}(θ)`.
+The phases in the last sum lie in an arc of width at most `π/2`, so
+`∫|h_θ'(u₀)|² dθ/(2π) ≥ t²n/4` by orthogonality of positive `y` frequencies.
+The lower bound and the second derivative bound imply
+`|h_θ'(u₀)|²≤2D²U(M+εU)`. Integrating, using
+`∫U≤2√(kn)` and `∫U²=4kn`, should yield
+
+`M ≥ [t²/(16D²√k) − π²D²√k/q²]√n`.
+
+Since `D≤3t/2`, the claimed constants follow if `q≥40t√k`.
+The two copies automatically satisfy the 2-run conditions because residual
+differences have absolute value at most `t/2` and nonzero quotient differences
+have magnitude at least `q−t/2>2t`.
+
+This route does not use P24 to separate the two copies. It uses positivity at
+all `q` lifted grid points and the exact zero of the common pair factor.

